1
00:00:03,054 --> 00:00:03,293
Pop!

2
00:00:03,343 --> 00:00:03,582
Pop!

3
00:00:03,632 --> 00:00:04,377
In the pot,

4
00:00:04,427 --> 00:00:07,989
the small hard kernels turn into big white clouds.

5
00:00:08,039 --> 00:00:09,917
What is going on in there?

6
00:00:10,725 --> 00:00:13,651
Mila looks at a kernel with a magnifying glass:

7
00:00:13,701 --> 00:00:16,247
a hard shell, all smooth, tightly closed.

8
00:00:16,297 --> 00:00:16,943
And inside?

9
00:00:16,993 --> 00:00:18,399
A little water, hidden.

10
00:00:18,449 --> 00:00:19,399
That's the key!

11
00:00:20,162 --> 00:00:21,676
Discovery mission!

12
00:00:24,192 --> 00:00:24,856
Mini mode!

13
00:00:24,906 --> 00:00:27,857
Inside the kernel: starch, a little water,

14
00:00:27,907 --> 00:00:29,1000
and all around, a solid shell.

15
00:00:30,050 --> 00:00:32,836
We heat it: the water turns into steam.

16
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:36,545
The steam wants to get out, but the shell is closed:

17
00:00:36,595 --> 00:00:38,205
the pressure rises and rises…

18
00:00:38,255 --> 00:00:41,402
At around one hundred eighty degrees, the shell cracks!

19
00:00:42,638 --> 00:00:44,633
All at once, the pressure drops:

20
00:00:44,683 --> 00:00:48,405
the soft starch puffs up like foam and hardens as it cools.

21
00:00:48,455 --> 00:00:50,181
A white flake, much bigger!

22
00:00:50,951 --> 00:00:52,796
And the kernels that don't pop?

23
00:00:52,846 --> 00:00:55,486
A cracked shell or a kernel that is too dry:

24
00:00:55,536 --> 00:00:58,237
the steam escapes, the pressure doesn't rise.

25
00:00:58,287 --> 00:00:58,715
No pop!

26
00:00:59,494 --> 00:01:01,647
That's why popcorn pops.

27
00:01:03,008 --> 00:01:06,354
The water in the kernel turns to steam, the pressure cracks the shell,

28
00:01:06,404 --> 00:01:08,054
and the starch puffs up into foam.

29
00:01:08,990 --> 00:01:09,863
With an adult:

30
00:01:09,913 --> 00:01:12,367
watch the kernels through a glass lid.

31
00:01:12,417 --> 00:01:13,356
Count the pops…

32
00:01:13,406 --> 00:01:16,174
and look for the hard shell on each flake!

33
00:01:16,961 --> 00:01:18,461
And what do we breathe?

34
00:01:18,511 --> 00:01:19,859
The answer tomorrow.
